  Hand-written sample of `xcrun xctrace export` with xpath '/trace-toc/run[1]/data/table[@schema="os-signpost"]'
  (xctrace 16.0, Xcode 26.6), in the same style as per-thread-export: row children are positional
  in <schema> column order, an empty cell is <sentinel/>, repeated values are interned (first
  occurrence id="N", later ones <tag ref="N"/>, inside metadata cells too), the emit-location
  column is elided, and the table is split over two <node> elements with only the first carrying
  <schema>.

  Shape: the fixture for the InboundChunk ceiling line. The other fixtures top out at 1500-byte
  chunks, so on them all five threshold shares are 0.000% / 0.00% and the threshold accumulation
  has no coverage. Here the seven chunk sizes straddle the five printed thresholds: one below
  64 KB (1448), one at each of 65536, 131072 and 262144, one between 262144 and 524288 (393216),
  and two at 524288 so the at-max count is not the degenerate 1. Only TransportRead and
  InboundChunk rows are present — one read and its chunk back to back on the single delivery
  thread NIO-SGLTN-1-#1 (0x101), as since the push-conversion (#45, 6.0.0-rc5), so the coalescing
  ratio is 1.00 and the ceiling line reads the receive length. There are deliberately no
  RecvDrain, ServiceDispatch or ServicePass rows: those lines print their empty forms and the
  fixture stays minimal. Run with scripts/profile-summary.sh in its default (per-thread) mode.

  Timeline (ns), subsystem ro.SimpleKube.AMSMB2 / category Inbound: seven pairs 1 ms apart, each
  chunk 0.100 ms after its read, from TransportRead 1448 @1.000000000 to InboundChunk 524288
  @1.006100000.

  Expected numbers (nearest-rank percentiles, 1-based index ceil(N*p/100)):
    TransportRead  n=7  bytes 1901992  sorted [1448,65536,131072,262144,393216,524288,524288]
                   -> min 1448, median idx4=262144, p95 idx7=524288, max 524288
    InboundChunk   n=7  bytes 1901992  same sizes -> same stats
    ceiling: max 524288, 2 chunks at it = 2/7 = 28.571% of chunks, 2*524288/1901992 = 55.13% of bytes
             >= 65536:   6/7 = 85.714% of chunks, 1900544/1901992 = 99.92% of bytes
             >= 131072:  5/7 = 71.429%,           1835008/1901992 = 96.48%
             >= 262144:  4/7 = 57.143%,           1703936/1901992 = 89.59%
             >= 524288:  2/7 = 28.571%,           1048576/1901992 = 55.13%
             >= 1048576: 0/7 =  0.000%,                          0 =  0.00%
    RecvDrain      n=0; ServiceDispatch n=0; ServicePass n=0
    ratio 7/7 = 1.00; 1 delivery thread (0x101); zero-byte skipped 0
    pump-hop: 7 pairs, every latency 0.100 ms, 0 chunks without a read, 0 reads without a chunk,
              0 pairing errors
    buffered 1901992 - 0 = 1901992
    span = active = 1.006100000-1.000000000 = 0.006100 s -> 0 drained bytes -> 0.000 MB/s
-->
